Keep a shared word as empty text.
Place "bccb" into word.
Keep a shared size as 0.
Set size to 4.
Keep a shared modulus as 0.
Set modulus to 1000000007.
Keep a shared table as an empty list of whole numbers.
For every spot from 0 to 15.
Place 0 into table.

Keep a shared firstspot as 0.
Keep a shared lastspot as 0.
To findfirst from spot (a whole number) with finish (a whole number) and target (a whole number).
If spot is at least finish, return.
The here is character spot of word.
If here is target, set firstspot to spot, return.
Findfirst from spot plus 1 with finish and target.

To findlast from spot (a whole number) with finish (a whole number) and target (a whole number).
If spot is less than finish, return.
The here is character spot of word.
If here is target, set lastspot to spot, return.
Findlast from spot minus 1 with finish and target.

To fold from start (a whole number) with span (a whole number) and width (a whole number).
The finish is start plus span minus 1.
The next is start plus 1.
The before is finish minus 1.
The inside is item (next times width plus finish) of table.
The below is item (start times width plus before) of table.
The overlap is item (next times width plus before) of table.
The value is inside plus below minus overlap.
Set value to value modulo modulus.
If value is less than 0, set value to value plus modulus.
Set item (start times width plus finish) of table to value.

To match from start (a whole number) with span (a whole number) and width (a whole number).
The finish is start plus span minus 1.
If span is 2, set item (start times width plus finish) of table to 2, return.
The next is start plus 1.
The before is finish minus 1.
The inside is item (next times width plus before) of table.
The value is inside times 2.
Set firstspot to -1.
Set lastspot to -2.
The target is character start of word.
Findfirst from next with finish and target.
Findlast from before with next and target.
If firstspot is less than 0, set value to value plus 2.
If firstspot is at least 0 and firstspot is lastspot, set value to value plus 1.
The leftcut is firstspot plus 1.
The rightcut is lastspot minus 1.
If firstspot is at least 0 and firstspot is not lastspot, set value to value minus item (leftcut times width plus rightcut) of table.
Set value to value modulo modulus.
If value is less than 0, set value to value plus modulus.
Set item (start times width plus finish) of table to value.

For every spot from 0 to 3.
Set item (spot times 4 plus spot) of table to 1.

For every span from 2 to 4.
For every start from 0 to 4 minus span.
The finish is start plus span minus 1.
The firstchar is character start of word.
The lastchar is character finish of word.
If firstchar is not lastchar, Fold from start with span and size.
If firstchar is lastchar, Match from start with span and size.

The last is size minus 1.
Show item last of table.
